{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219111718,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2cf0b001od1zqQ26FgNpcW","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2b8e60012Ff0O0tKhOGcBp","type":"tool","callID":"call_e51f47cd94584b8cbbbc3765","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","offset":1130},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1130: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1131: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1132: - All 341 tests passing\n1133: \n1134: **Technical Decisions:**\n1135: \n1136: - Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n1137: - Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n1138: - Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n1139: - Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n1140: - Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n1141: - Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n1142: - Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n1143: \n1144: **Test Coverage:**\n1145: \n1146: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1147: - Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n1148: - Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n1149: \n1150: **Implementation Summary (Export/Import JSON):**\n1151: \n1152: - Implemented Export JSON button in SettingsPanel footer\n1153: - Implemented Import JSON button with hidden file input\n1154: - Export creates downloadable JSON file (gol-expert-settings.json)\n1155: - Import loads JSON file with validation\n1156: - Comprehensive validation for all expert settings parameters\n1157: - Error message display for invalid imports\n1158: - File format: JSON with pretty-printing (2-space indentation)\n1159: - Blob-based file download with URL.createObjectURL\n1160: - FileReader API for file upload\n1161: - All 349 tests passing\n1162: \n1163: **Technical Decisions:**\n1164: \n1165: - Export uses Blob and URL.createObjectURL for download\n1166: - Pretty-printed JSON with 2-space indentation\n1167: - Import validates against all parameter ranges\n1168: - Custom validation function returns detailed error messages\n1169: - Hidden file input triggered via button click\n1170: - Error state managed in component state\n1171: - Invalid settings prevent import with user feedback\n1172: \n1173: **Validation Coverage:**\n1174: \n1175: - Movement detection: centroidHistoryLength (3-10), movementThreshold (0.1-2.0), minClusterSize (1-5)\n1176: - Scoring: moverPointsPerGeneration (1-100), oscillatorPointsPerGeneration (0-20), scoreMultiplier (0.1-5.0)\n1177: - Level generation: baseTimeSeconds (10-120), timeIncrementPerLevel (0-60), baseFlux (5-50), difficultyScalingMode (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n1178: - Grid sizing: mobileCellSize (14-24), desktopCellSize (16-28), minVisibleCells (≥1)\n1179: - Audio: enabled (boolean), volume (0-0.5), waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1180: \n1181: **Test Coverage:**\n1182: \n1183: - All existing 349 tests continue to pass\n1184: - Export functionality verified through manual testing\n1185: - Import functionality verified with valid and invalid JSON files\n1186: - Error handling tested for malformed JSON\n1187: \n1188: ### 5.2 Presets System (LOW - Convenience)\n1189: \n1190: - [x] Implement preset configurations\n1191:   - Easy: Lower difficulty, generous resources\n1192:   - Normal: Balanced gameplay\n1193:   - Hard: Strict time/flux limits\n1194:   - Chaos: Extreme parameters, unpredictable\n1195: - [x] Implement preset selection UI\n1196:   - Dropdown in Expert Settings\n1197:   - Preview preset values\n1198: - [ ] Add custom preset support\n1199:   - Allow users to save current settings as preset\n1200:   - Name and save custom configurations\n1201:   - NOT YET IMPLEMENTED\n1202: \n1203: **Dependencies**: Expert settings\n1204: \n1205: **Implementation Summary:**\n1206: \n1207: - Implemented Preset type in src/types/index.ts with four preset options: EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS\n1208: - Implemented src/lib/presets.ts library with applyPreset(), getPresetDescription(), and preset configurations\n1209: - Created four preset configurations with balanced parameter sets:\n1210:   - EASY: Generous Flux (30), longer time limits (90s), lenient scoring (15pt movers, 3pt oscillators), lower movement threshold (0.3)\n1211:   - NORMAL: Balanced Flux (20), standard time limits (60s), standard scoring (10pt movers, 2pt oscillators), standard movement threshold (0.5)\n1212:   - HARD: Limited Flux (15), shorter time limits (40s), strict scoring (8pt movers, 1pt oscillators), higher movement threshold (0.7)\n1213:   - CHAOS: Extreme Flux (10), very short time limits (30s), chaotic scoring (5pt movers, 1pt oscillators), low movement threshold (0.1), larger grid sizing (28px desktop, 22px mobile)\n1214: - Updated SettingsPanel.tsx to include preset selector with description at top of panel\n1215: - Updated SettingsPanel.css with preset section styling\n1216: - Updated createInitialExpertSettings() in src/lib/state.ts to use NORMAL preset by default\n1217: - Added comprehensive test suite with 11 tests covering all presets and edge cases\n1218: - All tests passing (360 total)\n1219: \n1220: **Technical Decisions:**\n1221: \n1222: - Preset type defined as enum-like string union: 'EASY' | 'NORMAL' | 'HARD' | 'CHAOS'\n1223: - applyPreset() performs deep clone using JSON.parse(JSON.stringify()) to prevent mutation issues\n1224: - getPresetDescription() returns human-readable description for each preset explaining the balance and intended difficulty\n1225: - Preset selector placed at top of SettingsPanel for easy access and visibility\n1226: - Preset descriptions use glassmorphism styling with subtle background for readability\n1227: - Default preset is NORMAL for balanced gameplay experience\n1228: - All preset parameters validated against spec-defined ranges\n1229: - Preset application immediately updates all expert settings without requiring panel close/reopen\n1230: - Preset configurations include all expert settings: movement detection, scoring, level generation, grid sizing, and audio parameters\n1231: \n1232: **Test Coverage: 11 tests**\n1233: \n1234: - Preset type definition: 1 test\n1235: - EASY preset configuration: 1 test\n1236: - NORMAL preset configuration: 1 test\n1237: - HARD preset configuration: 1 test\n1238: - CHAOS preset configuration: 1 test\n1239: - applyPreset() deep clone behavior: 1 test\n1240: - applyPreset() applies correct values: 1 test\n1241: - getPresetDescription() returns correct descriptions: 3 tests (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS)\n1242: - Invalid preset handling: 1 test\n1243: \n1244: **Integration Notes:**\n1245: \n1246: - Presets integrated into SettingsPanel as dropdown selector at top of panel\n1247: - Preset selector onChange handler calls applyPreset() to update expert settings\n1248: - Preset descriptions displayed below selector to explain each preset's characteristics\n1249: - createInitialExpertSettings() now uses applyPreset('NORMAL') for default configuration\n1250: - Preset system works seamlessly with existing settings persistence (localStorage)\n1251: - Users can manually tweak parameters after selecting a preset for further customization\n1252: - Total test count: 360 tests passing (up from 349)\n1253: \n1254: **Implementation Summary (Tooltips/Documentation & Danger Zone):**\n1255: \n1256: - Added comprehensive help text for all expert settings parameters\n1257: - Each setting now has italicized help text explaining its purpose and valid range\n1258: - Added danger zone section at bottom of settings panel with red warning theme\n1259: - Implemented Chaos Multiplier control (0.5-10.0x) for scoring difficulty scaling\n1260: - Implemented Timer Speed control (0.5-5.0x) for level time countdown speed\n1261: - Updated ExpertSettings type to include optional chaosMultiplier and timerSpeed fields\n1262: - Updated all preset configurations (EASY, NORMAL, HARD, CHAOS) with danger zone defaults\n1263: - Added validation for danger zone parameters in both SettingsPanel.tsx and settings.ts\n1264: - Added CSS styling for danger zone with warning banner and red-themed controls\n1265: - All 360 tests passing\n1266: \n1267: **Technical Decisions:**\n1268: \n1269: - Help text uses italicized styling with reduced opacity for subtle readability\n1270: - Danger zone placed at bottom of settings panel with distinct visual styling\n1271: - Red border and warning banner signal extreme/dangerous settings\n1272: - Danger zone controls use red-themed slider thumbs for visual distinction\n1273: - Defaults: chaosMultiplier=1.0, timerSpeed=1.0 for balanced gameplay\n1274: - Preset danger zone values: EASY (0.5x, 0.8x), NORMAL (1.0x, 1.0x), HARD (1.5x, 1.5x), CHAOS (3.0x, 2.5x)\n1275: - Optional fields in ExpertSettings type (chaosMultiplier?, timerSpeed?) for backward compatibility\n1276: - Validation prevents extreme values: chaosMultiplier (0.5-10.0), timerSpeed (0.5-5.0)\n1277: \n1278: **Test Coverage:**\n1279: \n1280: - All existing 360 tests continue to pass\n1281: - Preset tests updated to include new danger zone fields\n1282: - Settings validation tests include danger zone parameter checks\n1283: - Integration verified through manual testing\n1284: \n1285: **Implementation Notes:**\n1286: \n1287: - Danger zone settings allow experienced players to customize extreme game modes\n1288: - Help text makes expert settings more accessible to new players\n1289: - Visual hierarchy separates normal settings from dangerous ones\n1290: - Changes propagate through existing preset and settings persistence systems\n1291: \n1292: ---\n1293: \n1294: ## Sprint 6: Quality Assurance\n1295: \n1296: _Goal: Stability, accessibility, and performance_\n1297: \n1298: ### 6.1 Error Handling & Resilience (MEDIUM - Stability)\n1299: \n1300: - [x] Implement global error boundary (COMPLETED 2026-02-16)\n1301:   - Catch React component errors\n1302:   - Display user-friendly error message\n1303:   - Log error details\n1304: - [x] Add input validation\n1305:   - Validate all user inputs\n1306:   - Validate configuration parameters\n1307:   - Prevent NaN and infinity\n1308: - [ ] Handle edge cases gracefully\n1309:   - Empty grid states\n1310:   - Zero flux scenarios\n1311:   - Invalid level numbers\n1312:   - Corrupted localStorage\n1313: - [ ] Add retry mechanisms\n1314:   - Retry failed operations with exponential backoff\n1315:   - Graceful degradation when features fail\n1316: - [ ] Handle browser compatibility\n1317:   - Check for required APIs (Web Audio, Canvas)\n1318:   - Fallbacks for unsupported features\n1319:   - Clear error messages\n1320: \n1321: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1322: \n1323: **Implementation Summary (Error Boundary):**\n1324: \n1325: - Implemented ErrorBoundary class component in src/components/ErrorBoundary.tsx with comprehensive error handling\n1326: - Implemented getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method to catch React errors and set error state\n1327: - Implemented componentDidCatch lifecycle method to log error details to console\n1328: - Implemented user-friendly error UI with \"Something went wrong\" message and reload button\n1329: - Implemented development-only error details section showing error message, component stack, and stack trace\n1330: - Created ErrorBoundary.css with glassmorphism styling matching application theme\n1331: - Added ErrorBoundary.test.tsx with 4 comprehensive tests covering all error scenarios\n1332: - Integrated ErrorBoundary into App.tsx to wrap all application components\n1333: - Error boundary displays reload button that refreshes the page to recover from errors\n1334: \n1335: **Technical Decisions:**\n1336: \n1337: - Used class component (instead of function component) to implement getDerivedStateFromError lifecycle method\n1338: - Error details only shown in development mode (import.meta.env.DEV) for security\n1339: - Reload button uses window.location.reload() to fully refresh the application state\n1340: - Console.error called with both error object and component stack for debugging\n1341: - Glassmorphism design matches other UI components for consistent look and feel\n1342: - Error boundary positioned with z-index: 999999 to overlay all content\n1343: \n1344: **Test Coverage: 4 tests**\n1345: \n1346: - ErrorBoundary renders children when no error occurs\n1347: - ErrorBoundary catches errors and displays error UI\n1348: - ErrorBoundary logs error and component stack to console\n1349: - ErrorBoundary reload button is clickable and displayed\n1350: \n1351: **Integration Notes:**\n1352: \n1353: - ErrorBoundary wraps entire App component to catch all React errors\n1354: - All 364 tests passing (including 4 new ErrorBoundary tests)\n1355: - Error boundary prevents white screen crashes by providing user-friendly error UI\n1356: - Development mode shows detailed error information for debugging\n1357: - Production mode shows simplified error message for better user experience\n1358: \n1359: ### 6.2 Accessibility (LOW - Inclusivity)\n1360: \n1361: - [ ] Implement keyboard navigation\n1362:   - Arrow keys for grid navigation\n1363:   - Enter/Space to place cells\n1364:   - Escape to cancel/close panels\n1365:   - Tab navigation through UI controls\n1366: - [ ] Add screen reader support\n1367:   - ARIA labels for UI elements\n1368:   - Announce game state changes\n1369:   - Alternative text for visual elements\n1370:   - Live regions for score/timer updates\n1371: - [x] Implement reduced motion support\n1372:   - Respect prefers-reduced-motion media query\n1373:   - Disable animations when requested\n1374:   - Simplified visual feedback\n1375: - [ ] Add high contrast mode\n1376:   - Toggle for high contrast colors\n1377:   - Larger text option\n1378:   - Improved readability\n1379: - [ ] Ensure minimum touch targets\n1380:   - 44×44px minimum for mobile\n1381:   - Spacious clickable areas\n1382: - [ ] Focus management\n1383:   - Visible focus indicators\n1384:   - Logical tab order\n1385:   - Focus trap in modals\n1386: \n1387: **Dependencies**: UI components, user interaction\n1388: \n1389: **Implementation Summary (Reduced Motion Support):**\n1390: \n1391: - Added @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) queries to all 10 CSS files\n1392: - Disabled all animations (keyframe animations, transition properties, transform animations) when reduced motion is preferred\n1393: - Covered 76 animation/transition instances across entire codebase\n1394: - Files updated: VictoryScreen.css, IntroOverlay.css, TransitionOverlay.css, SettingsPanel.css, GlassHUD.css, ScoreDisplay.css, LevelStats.css, FluxDisplay.css, index.css, ErrorBoundary.css\n1395: - Prioritized disabling infinite animations (glitch, pulse-glow, pulse) as they cause most vestibular issues\n1396: - Simplified visual feedback for users with motion sensitivity by removing all motion\n1397: - All 364 tests passing with reduced motion support enabled\n1398: \n1399: **Technical Decisions:**\n1400: \n1401: - Used CSS @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) query to detect user's motion preference\n1402: - Set animation: none and transition: none for all animated elements when reduced motion is preferred\n1403: - Set transform: none for hover/active states to prevent scale animations\n1404: - Applied overrides at end of each CSS file to ensure they take precedence\n1405: - Maintains full functionality while removing all motion effects\n1406: - Respects OS-level accessibility settings for users with vestibular disorders or motion sensitivity\n1407: \n1408: ### 6.3 Performance Optimization (LOW - Performance)\n1409: \n1410: - [ ] Implement performance monitoring\n1411:   - FPS counter (development only)\n1412:   - Memory usage tracking\n1413:   - Component render profiling\n1414: - [ ] Add performance optimizations\n1415:   - Memoize expensive calculations\n1416:   - Virtualize large lists (if applicable)\n1417:   - Lazy load non-critical components\n1418:   - Debounce/throttle frequent operations\n1419: - [ ] Profile and optimize\n1420:   - Identify performance bottlenecks\n1421:   - Optimize critical paths\n1422:   - Ensure 60fps with 500+ cells\n1423:   - Test on low-end devices\n1424: - [ ] Implement lazy loading\n1425:   - Load audio on first interaction\n1426:   - Lazy load expert settings panel\n1427:   - Code splitting for production\n1428: \n1429: **Dependencies**: All systems\n1430: \n1431: ### 6.4 Testing (LOW - Quality Assurance)\n1432: \n1433: - [ ] Set up testing framework\n1434:   - Choose testing framework (Vitest recommended)\n1435:   - Configure test environment\n1436:   - Set up coverage reporting\n1437: - [ ] Write unit tests for simulation engine\n1438:   - Rule application (born/survive)\n1439:   - Toroidal boundaries\n1440:   - Age tracking\n1441:   - Edge cases (empty grid, static patterns)\n1442: - [ ] Write unit tests for phase management\n1443:   - Phase transitions\n1444:   - Guard conditions\n1445:   - Timer accuracy\n1446: - [ ] Write unit tests for flux management\n1447:   - Placement and refund logic\n1448:   - Phase-based behavior\n1449: - [ ] Write unit tests for movement detection\n1450:   - Connected component detection\n1451:   - Centroid tracking\n1452:   - Classification accuracy\n1453: - [ ] Write unit tests for scoring system\n1454:   - Score calculation accuracy\n1455:   - Score cap handling\n1456:   - High score persistence\n1457: - [ ] Write unit tests for level progression\n1458:   - Level configuration generation\n1459:   - Difficulty scaling\n1460: - [ ] Write integration tests\n1461:   - End-to-end game flow\n1462:   - Level progression\n1463:   - Score calculation\n1464:   - UI interaction\n1465: - [ ] Add manual testing procedures\n1466:   - Mobile responsiveness\n1467:   - Touch interaction\n1468:   - Audio on different browsers\n1469:   - Performance with high cell counts\n1470:   - Accessibility testing\n1471: \n1472: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1473: \n1474: ### 6.5 Documentation (LOW - Knowledge Transfer)\n1475: \n1476: - [ ] Write README.md\n1477:   - Project overview\n1478:   - Installation instructions\n1479:   - Controls and gameplay guide\n1480:   - Configuration options\n1481:   - Known issues and limitations\n1482: - [ ] Add code comments\n1483:   - Complex algorithms (movement detection, simulation)\n1484:   - State machine logic\n1485:   - Performance-critical sections\n1486: - [ ] Document API interfaces\n1487:   - Component props\n1488:   - Utility functions\n1489:   - Configuration schemas\n1490:   - Type definitions\n1491: - [ ] Create developer guide\n1492:   - Architecture overview\n1493:   - How to add new features\n1494:   - Debugging tips\n1495:   - Common patterns\n1496: - [ ] Document expert settings\n1497:   - Each parameter explanation\n1498:   - Recommended values\n1499:   - Impact on gameplay\n1500: \n1501: **Dependencies**: All implemented systems\n1502: \n1503: ### 6.6 Code Quality & Refinement (COMPLETED - 2026-02-16)\n1504: \n1505: **Goal**: Fix lint errors, improve code quality, and ensure production readiness\n1506: \n1507: - [x] Fixed lint errors and code quality issues\n1508: - [x] Fixed clearTimeout not being recognized as global (changed to window.clearTimeout)\n1509: - [x] Added missing globals to ESLint config (Blob, URL, FileReader, HTMLInputElement)\n1510: - [x] Created separate vitest.config.ts to fix build error\n1511: - [x] Fixed 'any' types in SettingsPanel component (use Record<string, unknown>)\n1512: - [x] Removed unused error variable in catch block\n1513: - [x] Fixed synchronous setState in effects for FluxDisplay, ScoreDisplay, and Game components\n1514: - [x] Refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1515: - [x] Added eslint rule override to allow 'any' types in test files\n1516: - [x] All verification completed (360 tests passing, build successful, TypeScript clean)\n1517: \n1518: **Implementation Summary:**\n1519: \n1520: - Fixed clearTimeout global recognition issue by using window.clearTimeout throughout codebase\n1521: - Added missing browser globals to ESLint configuration: Blob, URL, FileReader, HTMLInputElement\n1522: - Created vitest.config.ts to separate test configuration from main Vite config, resolving build conflicts\n1523: - Replaced 'any' types in SettingsPanel component with Record<string, unknown> for proper type safety\n1524: - Removed unused error variable from catch block to satisfy ESLint no-unused-vars rule\n1525: - Fixed synchronous setState warnings in React effects:\n1526:   - FluxDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1527:   - ScoreDisplay: wrapped setState in useCallback with proper dependency tracking\n1528:   - Game: refactored levelStats from state to computed value using useMemo\n1529: - Added eslint rule override for test files to allow 'any' types when needed for test doubles\n1530: \n1531: **Technical Decisions:**\n1532: \n1533: - Used window.clearTimeout to ensure global recognition across all environments\n1534: - Created separate vitest.config.ts to isolate test environment configuration from production build\n1535: - Record<string, unknown> provides better type safety than 'any' while maintaining flexibility\n1536: - useMemo for levelStats prevents unnecessary re-computation and state updates\n1537: - useCallback for setState functions ensures stable references across renders\n1538: - ESLint overrides for test files scoped to .test.ts and .spec.ts extensions only\n1539: \n1540: **Verification Results:**\n1541: \n1542: - All 360 tests passing\n1543: - Build successful (npm run build)\n1544: - TypeScript compilation clean (npm run typecheck)\n1545: - ESLint passing (npm run lint)\n1546: - Git tag 0.1.5 created and pushed\n1547: \n1548: ---\n1549: \n1550: ## Parallel Development Tracks\n1551: \n1552: ### Track A (Can start after Project Setup):\n1553: \n1554: - Type definitions → Shared utilities → All other systems\n1555: \n1556: ### Track B (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1557: \n1558: - Phase Management → UI Overlay → Phase Status Display\n1559: - Canvas Rendering → Grid Interaction\n1560: \n1561: ### Track C (Can start after Simulation Engine):\n1562: \n1563: - User Interaction → Audio Sonification → Visual Polish\n1564: - Flux Management → Grid Interaction\n1565: \n1566: ### Track D (Can start after Canvas Rendering + User Interaction + Flux Management):\n1567: \n1568: - Grid Integration → Playable MVP\n1569: \n1570: ### Track E (Can start after MVP):\n1571: \n1572: - Intro Overlay → Main UI Controls → Settings Panel\n1573: - Movement Detection → Scoring System → Level Progression\n1574: \n1575: ### Track F (Can start after Level Progression):\n1576: \n1577: - Transition System → Victory Screen\n1578: \n1579: ### Track G (Can start after Scoring + Level Progression):\n1580: \n1581: - Audio Sonification → Visual Polish → Mobile Enhancements\n1582: \n1583: ### Track H (Can start after all features):\n1584: \n1585: - Expert Settings → Presets → Error Handling → Accessibility → Performance → Testing → Documentation\n1586: \n1587: ---\n1588: \n1589: ## Critical Path (Sequential Must-Haves for MVP):\n1590: \n1591: 1. **Project Setup** → Build system\n1592: 2. **Type Definitions** → All type-safe development\n1593: 3. **Shared Utilities** → Validation and state management\n1594: 4. **Simulation Engine** → Core gameplay logic\n1595: 5. **Phase Management with COUNTDOWN** → Game flow control\n1596: 6. **Canvas Rendering** → Visual feedback\n1597: 7. **User Interaction** → Input handling\n1598: 8. **Flux Management** → Resource system\n1599: 9. **Grid Integration** → Playable MVP\n1600: \n1601: ## Testing Milestones:\n1602: \n1603: - **After Sprint 1**: MVP manually playable (place cells, watch simulation, all phases work)\n1604: - **After Sprint 2**: Full game UI (intro, controls, scoring, settings)\n1605: - **After Sprint 3**: Complete game loop (intro → levels → transitions → victory)\n1606: - **After Sprint 4**: Audio and polish (all sounds, visual enhancements, mobile support)\n1607: - **After Sprint 5**: Expert settings and customization\n1608: - **After Sprint 6**: Production-ready with stability, accessibility, performance, tests, and docs\n1609: \n1610: ## Success Criteria:\n1611: \n1612: - [ ] Playable MVP after Sprint 1 (can place cells and run simulation with all phases)\n1613: - [ ] Complete UI after Sprint 2 (intro, controls, settings)\n1614: - [ ] Full game loop after Sprint 3 (intro → levels → scoring → transitions → victory)\n1615: - [ ] Audio and polish after Sprint 4 (all sounds, animations, mobile support)\n1616: - [ ] All features implemented after Sprint 5 (expert settings, presets)\n1617: - [ ] Production-ready after Sprint 6 (stability, accessibility, performance, tests, docs)\n1618: - [ ] 60fps performance with 500+ cells\n1619: - [ ] Works on mobile and desktop\n1620: - [ ] Audio works across all major browsers\n1621: - [ ] No console errors or warnings in production\n1622: - [ ] High score persistence works\n1623: - [ ] Expert settings properly configure all systems\n1624: - [ ] All critical edge cases handled gracefully\n1625: - [ ] Accessible keyboard navigation\n1626: - [ ] Comprehensive test coverage for core systems\n1627: - [ ] Clear documentation for developers and players\n1628: \n1629: ## Framework Decisions (MAKE THESE FIRST):\n1630: \n1631: - **Framework**: React/Vite (recommended for performance and DX)\n1632: - **State Management**: React hooks (useState, useReducer, useRef) - minimal, no external library needed\n1633: - **Styling**: CSS modules or vanilla CSS with CSS variables for theming\n1634: - **Testing**: Vitest (fast, compatible with Vite)\n1635: - **Build Tool**: Vite (recommended for speed and simplicity)\n1636: \n1637: ## Implementation Order Recommendations:\n1638: \n1639: ### Week 1: Foundation\n1640: \n1641: 1. Project setup (Day 1)\n1642: 2. Type definitions (Day 1)\n1643: 3. Shared utilities (Day 2)\n1644: 4. Simulation engine (Day 2-3)\n1645: 5. Phase management with COUNTDOWN (Day 3-4)\n1646: 6. Canvas rendering (Day 4)\n1647: \n1648: ### Week 2: Interaction & UI\n1649: \n1650: 7. User interaction (Day 1)\n1651: 8. Flux management (Day 1-2)\n1652: 9. Grid interaction (Day 2) - MVP milestone reached\n1653: 10. Intro overlay (Day 3)\n1654: 11. Main UI controls (Day 3-4)\n1655: 12. Phase status display (Day 4)\n1656: \n1657: ### Week 3: Scoring & Progression\n1658: \n1659: 13. Movement detection (Day 1-2)\n1660: 14. Scoring system (Day 2-3)\n1661: 15. Settings panel (Day 3)\n1662: 16. Level progression (Day 4)\n1663: \n1664: ### Week 4: Transitions & Audio\n1665: \n1666: 17. Transition system (Day 1-2)\n1667: 18. Victory screen (Day 2)\n1668: 19. Audio sonification (Day 3-4)\n1669: 20. Visual polish (Day 4)\n1670: \n1671: ### Week 5: Advanced Features\n1672: \n1673: 21. Expert settings (Day 1-3)\n1674: 22. Mobile enhancements (Day 3)\n1675: 23. Presets system (Day 4)\n1676: \n1677: ### Week 6: Quality Assurance\n1678: \n1679: 24. Error handling (Day 1)\n1680: 25. Accessibility (Day 1-2)\n1681: 26. Performance optimization (Day 2)\n1682: 27. Testing (Day 3-4)\n1683: 28. Documentation (Day 4)\n1684: \n1685: ## Notes:\n1686: \n1687: - Update status (checkmark) as tasks are completed\n1688: - The plan is prioritized: CRITICAL first, then HIGH, MEDIUM, LOW\n1689: - Parallel tracks enable concurrent work where dependencies allow\n1690: - Focus on MVP first, then incrementally add polish\n1691: - src/lib/ is project's standard library for shared utilities\n1692: - Prefer consolidated implementations in src/lib/ over ad-hoc copies\n1693: - Always run lint and typecheck commands after completing features\n1694: - Test on both desktop and mobile throughout development\n1695: - Gather user feedback during development to improve UX\n1696: - Document decisions and trade-offs in comments or docs\n1697: - Keep code modular and maintainable for future enhancements\n1698: \n1699: ## Recent Progress:\n1700: \n1701: **Current Status (2026-02-16):**\n1702: \n1703: - **Sprint 1-5 Complete**: MVP, scoring, levels, transitions, audio, visual polish, mobile, and expert settings fully implemented\n1704: - **Sprint 6 In Progress**: Error Boundary completed, remaining items (accessibility, performance, testing, documentation) pending\n1705: - **All 364 tests passing** with comprehensive coverage of implemented features\n1706: - **Production-ready core game** with complete feature set\n1707: \n1708: **Recent Completion:**\n1709: \n1710: - **Sprint 6.1 Error Boundary**: Implemented global error boundary with user-friendly error UI, development-mode error details, and reload functionality. All 4 tests passing.\n1711: \n1712: ---\n1713: \n1714: **Documentation Update (2026-02-16):**\n1715: \n1716: - Updated IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md to mark Error Boundary as complete (Sprint 6.1, lines 1300-1303)\n1717: - Cleaned up Recent Progress section by removing outdated turn summaries\n1718: - Consolidated progress notes for better readability and maintainability\n1719: - Documentation now reflects current implementation state accurately\n1720: \n1721: ---\n1722: \n1723: **Turn Summary (2026-02-16):**\n1724: \n1725: - **Error Boundary (v0.0.1)**: Implemented global error boundary in Sprint 6.1 with user-friendly error UI, development-mode error details, reload functionality, and 4 tests passing\n1726: - **Reduced Motion Support (v0.0.2)**: Implemented accessibility support in Sprint 6.2 by adding prefers-reduced-motion media queries to all 10 CSS files, disabling 76 animation/transition instances for users with motion sensitivity\n1727: \n\n(End of file - total 1727 lines)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"- Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n- Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n- All 341 tests passing\n\n**Technical Decisions:**\n\n- Uses useRef for tap tracking (avoid re-renders)\n- Implements resetTapState function inside useEffect closure for access to refs\n- Configurable threshold zone for corner detection\n- Supports both touch (touchstart) and mouse (click) events\n- Prevents default on touch events to avoid conflicts with game controls\n- Cleanup removes event listeners and clears timeout\n- Time window: 500ms between taps (standard gesture timing)\n\n**Test Coverage:**\n\n- All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n- Gesture detection verified through manual testing\n- Hook follows React best practices for event handling\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219111693,"end":1771219111715}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219111722,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2cf10001Mh0EIlGjwYAmS8","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2b8e60012Ff0O0tKhOGcBp","type":"tool","callID":"call_94e04dd2c18e4512ad40d745","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/auto-advance-transitions.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/auto-advance-transitions.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Auto-Advance Transitions\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Seamless level progression system with cinematic fade transitions between completed levels.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Transition Trigger\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface TransitionConfig {\n11:   fadeOutDuration: number;        // Default: 2.0s\n12:   fadeInDuration: number;         // Default: 2.0s\n13:   interstitialDuration: number;   // Default: 2.0s (black screen)\n14:   autoAdvanceDelay: number;       // Default: 2.0s (time on finished screen)\n15:   skipEnabled: boolean;            // Allow skipping transitions (Space/ESC)\n16: }\n17: ```\n18: \n19: ```typescript\n20: type TransitionState = \n21:   | 'PLAYING'           // Normal gameplay\n22:   | 'FADING_OUT'        // Fade to black\n23:   | 'INTERSTITIAL'      // Black screen, show level info\n24:   | 'FADING_IN'         // Fade from black\n25:   | 'READY';            // Next level loaded, waiting for input\n26: ```\n27: \n28: ### Transition Sequence\n29: \n30: #### FINISHED → Next Level (Success)\n31: 1. **FINISHED Phase Display** (2.0s):\n32:    - Show final score\n33:    - Show \"Level Complete\" text\n34:    - Continue rendering simulation (visual only, no scoring)\n35:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to fade out immediately\n36: \n37: 2. **Fade Out** (2.0s):\n38:    - Full-screen black overlay opacity 0→1\n39:    - Easing: ease-in-out\n40:    - Simulation continues but hidden\n41:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to interstitial immediately\n42: \n43: 3. **Interstitial** (2.0s):\n44:    - Full black screen\n45:    - Center: \"Level X Complete\" (fading out)\n46:    - Center: \"Level X+1\" (fading in)\n47:    - Load next level configuration\n48:    - Reset game state (Flux, Score resets - no carryover between levels)\n49:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to fade in immediately\n50: \n51: 4. **Fade In** (2.0s):\n52:    - Black overlay opacity 1→0\n53:    - New level visible with fresh grid\n54:    - Simulation stopped, waiting for countdown to finish\n55:    - PLANNING phase ready after countdown\n56:    - **SKIP**: Press Space/ESC to skip to READY immediately\n57: \n58: 5. **READY**:\n59:    - Player can immediately start placing cells\n60: \n61: #### FINISHED → Game Over (Failure)\n62: - Similar fade sequence but to \"Game Over\" screen\n63: - Option to \"Retry Level\" or \"Return to Menu\"\n64: - No auto-advance on failure (wait for input)\n65: \n66: ## UI/UX Requirements\n67: \n68: ### Fade Overlay\n69: - **Element**: Fixed position div covering viewport\n70: - **Color**: Black (#000000)\n71: - **Z-Index**: Above all game elements, below modals\n72: - **Pointer Events**: None (let clicks pass through if needed)\n73: \n74: ### Interstitial Display\n75: - **Level Complete Text**: \"Level X Complete\" - fade out during fade-to-black\n76: - **Next Level Text**: \"Level X+1\" - fade in during fade-from-black\n77: - **Font**: Large, bold, centered\n78: - **Optional**: Show quick stats (\"Score: Y\")\n79: \n80: ### Skip Indicator\n81: - **Prompt**: \"Press Space or ESC to skip\" (small text at bottom)\n82: - **Visibility**: Shown during all transition phases\n83: - **Fade out**: Hide during READY state\n84: \n85: ### Audio\n86: - **Fade Out**: \"Level Complete\" chime/sound\n87: - **Interstitial**: Brief ambient or silence\n88: - **Fade In**: \"Level Start\" sound (distinct from first level)\n89: \n90: ### Visual Effects\n91: - **Blur**: Slight blur on game during fade (optional polish)\n92: - **Progress**: Optional progress bar showing \"X of Y levels\"\n93: \n94: ## Edge Cases\n95: \n96:  1. **Browser Tab During Transition**: If user switches tabs mid-transition:\n97:      - Pause transition timer to prevent level from advancing unseen\n98:      - Resume when tab becomes active again\n99:      - Note: This only applies to transitions - during gameplay, the game timer continues running when tab is inactive\n100: \n101:  2. **Rapid Success**: Player beating levels very quickly:\n102:      - Skip mechanism prevents transitions from feeling tedious\n103:      - Allow holding Space/ESC to skip all transitions\n104: \n105:  3. **Last Level**: After final level:\n106:      - Fade to \"Victory\" screen instead of next level\n107:      - Show total score accumulated across all levels\n108:      - Provide \"Play Again\" or \"Return to Level 1\"\n109: \n110:  4. **Interruption**: Player presses key during transition:\n111:      - Space/Escape: Skip to end of transition (immediately jump to READY state)\n112:      - Skip works at any point during transition sequence\n113: \n114:  5. **Performance**: Low-end devices might struggle with opacity animations:\n115:      - Use CSS `will-change: opacity`\n116:      - Consider reducing animation complexity\n117: \n118: ## Implementation Notes\n119: \n120: - Use CSS transitions for smooth 60fps fades\n121: - React state machine for transition phases\n122: - Preload next level assets during fade-out if possible\n123: - Audio: Fade volume during transition (not abrupt cut)\n124: - Mobile: Ensure transitions work with reduced motion preferences (accessibility)\n125: - Skip transitions configurable in Expert Settings\n126: - Test with all browser zoom levels to ensure overlay covers fully\n127: \n\n(End of file - total 127 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/auto-advance-transitions.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Auto-Advance Transitions\n\n## Overview\nSeamless level progression system with cinematic fade transitions between completed levels.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Transition Trigger\n```typescript\ninterface TransitionConfig {\n  fadeOutDuration: number;        // Default: 2.0s\n  fadeInDuration: number;         // Default: 2.0s\n  interstitialDuration: number;   // Default: 2.0s (black screen)\n  autoAdvanceDelay: number;       // Default: 2.0s (time on finished screen)\n  skipEnabled: boolean;            // Allow skipping transitions (Space/ESC)\n}\n```\n\n```typescript\ntype TransitionState = ","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219111698,"end":1771219111719}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219111724,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2cf180010wpws8b34OeIsi","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2b8e60012Ff0O0tKhOGcBp","type":"tool","callID":"call_638d11b95a9746d89fbeda9f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/level-progression.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/level-progression.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Level Progression\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Progressive difficulty system where players advance through levels with increasing time limits and limited Flux. The goal is to maximize points within each level's time limit and Flux budget.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Level Configuration Schema\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface LevelConfig {\n11:   levelNumber: number;\n12:   timeLimitSeconds: number;    // Increases with each level\n13:   initialFlux: number;          // Flux available for the level\n14: }\n15: \n16: interface LevelProgression {\n17:   currentLevel: number;\n18:   maxUnlockedLevel: number;      // For future: level select screen\n19:   totalScore: number;            // Cumulative score across all levels\n20:   levels: LevelConfig[];         // Array of level definitions\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ### Difficulty Scaling (Expert Settings Configurable)\n25: Default strategy: **Increase time for difficulty**\n26: \n27: ```typescript\n28: const defaultLevelGeneration = (levelNum: number): LevelConfig => ({\n29:   levelNumber: levelNum,\n30:   timeLimitSeconds: 45 + (levelNum - 1) * 15,  // 45, 60, 75, 90...\n31:   initialFlux: 20                            // Constant for now\n32: });\n33: ```\n34: \n35: Alternative strategies (selectable in Expert Settings):\n36: - **Time Only**: Increase time, constant Flux\n37: - **Resource Only**: Constant time, decrease Flux\n38: - **Mixed**: Both time and Flux adjusted\n39: - **Extreme**: Increase time slightly but aggressively reduce Flux\n40: \n41: ### Progression Flow\n42: 1. Player completes level N (timer reaches 0 or all cells die)\n43: 2. Screen fades out over 2.0s\n44: 3. Loading/interstitial (2.0s)\n45: 4. Screen fades in to level N+1 with fresh grid\n46: 5. Reset to PLANNING phase with fresh Flux\n47: 6. Score accumulated across all levels\n48: \n49: ### Game Objective\n50: - **Goal**: Maximize points within time limit and Flux budget\n51: - **Score Calculation**: Based on kinetic energy, cell activity, and survival (see scoring-system.md)\n52: - **Level Completion**: Timer reaches 0 OR all cells die (score stops accumulating)\n53: - **No Lose Condition**: Game always advances to next level; only score accumulation varies\n54: \n55: ## UI/UX Requirements\n56: \n57: ### Level Display\n58: - **Current Level**: Show \"Level X\" in corner of screen\n59: - **Progress**: Optional progress bar showing X of Y levels\n60: - **Level Complete**: Brief \"Level X Complete\" message during transition\n61: \n62: ### Transition Effects\n63: - **Fade Out**: 2.0s ease-out to black\n64: - **Interstitial**: Level number display (2.0s)\n65: - **Fade In**: 2.0s ease-in from black\n66: - **Sound**: Transition whoosh/complete sound effect\n67: - **Skip**: Press Space/ESC to skip to next level immediately\n68: \n69: ### End of Game\n70: - After final level (configurable, default 10), show victory screen\n71: - Display total accumulated score across all levels\n72: - Option to restart from level 1 or return to menu\n73: \n74: ## Edge Cases\n75: \n76: 1. **Level 0 or Invalid**: Default to level 1 if undefined\n77: 2. **Last Level**: Show victory screen with total score\n78: 3. **Browser Refresh**: Save progress in localStorage? (Optional persistence)\n79: 4. **All Cells Die Early**: Level ends immediately, score stops accumulating, game advances to next level\n80: \n81: ## Implementation Notes\n82: \n83: - Store level configs in JSON or TypeScript object\n84: - Generate levels dynamically or use static array\n85: - Total levels configurable in Expert Settings\n86: - Level progression increments on level completion (no win/lose condition)\n87: - Score accumulates across all levels (totalScore tracked separately)\n88: - Fade transitions use CSS opacity with 2s duration\n89: - Simulation stops when level ends, starts fresh for next level (no carryover)\n90: \n\n(End of file - total 90 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/level-progression.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Level Progression\n\n## Overview\nProgressive difficulty system where players advance through levels with increasing time limits and limited Flux. The goal is to maximize points within each level's time limit and Flux budget.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Level Configuration Schema\n```typescript\ninterface LevelConfig {\n  levelNumber: number;\n  timeLimitSeconds: number;    // Increases with each level\n  initialFlux: number;          // Flux available for the level\n}\n\ninterface LevelProgression {\n  currentLevel: number;\n  maxUnlockedLevel: number;      // For future: level select screen\n  totalScore: number;            // Cumulative score across all levels\n  levels: LevelConfig[];         // Array of level definitions","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219111706,"end":1771219111723}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219111728,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2cf14001weGq7N8slWAbe6","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2b8e60012Ff0O0tKhOGcBp","type":"tool","callID":"call_62acd2799ced45d2a5cc807e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/expert-settings.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Hidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Access Methods\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n11:   keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n12:   menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n13:   gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n14: }\n15: ```\n16: \n17: ### Configurable Parameters\n18: \n19: #### Movement Detection Parameters\n20: ```typescript\n21: interface MovementDetectionParams {\n22:   centroidHistoryLength: number;       // Generations to track (default: 5, range: 3-10)\n23:   movementThreshold: number;           // Cells to be \"moving\" (default: 0.5, range: 0.1-2.0)\n24:   minClusterSize: number;            // Minimum cells to track (default: 1, range: 1-5)\n25: }\n26: ```\n27: \n28: #### Scoring Parameters\n29: ```typescript\n30: interface ScoringParams {\n31:   moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n32:   oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n33:   scoreMultiplier: number;                // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n34: }\n35: ```\n36: \n37: #### Level Generation Parameters\n38: ```typescript\n39: interface LevelGenerationParams {\n40:   baseTimeSeconds: number;                // Default: 45, range: 10-120\n41:   timeIncrementPerLevel: number;          // Default: 15, range: 0-60\n42:   baseFlux: number;                       // Default: 20, range: 5-50\n43:   difficultyScalingMode: 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME';\n44: }\n45: ```\n46: \n47: #### Grid Sizing Parameters\n48: ```typescript\n49: interface GridSizingParams {\n50:   mobileCellSize: number;                 // Default: 18, range: 14-24\n51:   desktopCellSize: number;                // Default: 20, range: 16-28\n52:   minVisibleCells: number;                // Default: 10, minimum cells visible\n53: }\n54: ```\n55: \n56: ### Settings Persistence\n57: - Save to localStorage under key `gol-expert-settings`\n58: - Load on app startup\n59: - \"Reset to Defaults\" button with confirmation\n60: - Export/Import settings as JSON (for sharing configurations)\n61: \n62: ## UI/UX Requirements\n63: \n64: ### Panel Layout\n65: - **Position**: Modal overlay, centered or right sidebar\n66: - **Sections**: Collapsible groups by category (Movement, Scoring, Levels, Grid)\n67: - **Controls**:\n68:   - Sliders for numeric ranges\n69:   - Number inputs for precise values\n70:   - Dropdowns for mode selection\n71: \n72: ### Real-Time Updates\n73: - Changes apply immediately (no restart required)\n74: - Visual indicator when value differs from default\n75: - \"Revert\" button per section\n76: - Live preview: Show parameter effects in real-time if possible\n77: \n78: ### Danger Zone\n79: - Separate section for \"Break Things\" settings\n80: - Require confirmation for extreme values\n81: - Show warning if settings would make game impossible\n82: \n83: ### Export/Import\n84: - \"Export JSON\" button downloads current config\n85: - \"Import JSON\" file picker loads config\n86: - Validate imported JSON against schema\n87: \n88: ## Edge Cases\n89: \n90: 1. **Invalid Values**: Input validation prevents negative numbers, out-of-range values\n91: 2. **Settings While Running**: Changes to scoring apply immediately; level changes apply on next level\n92: 3. **Reset During Game**: Reset to defaults should warn if game in progress\n93: 4. **Corrupted Storage**: If localStorage has invalid JSON, fall back to defaults\n94: 5. **Mobile Access**: Ensure gesture detection doesn't conflict with game controls\n95: \n96: ## Implementation Notes\n97: \n98: - Use React Context or Zustand for settings state\n99: - Validate all inputs with constraints\n100: - Schema validation using Zod or similar\n101: - Default values should create balanced, playable game\n102: - Consider \"Presets\" dropdown (\"Easy\", \"Normal\", \"Hard\", \"Chaos\")\n103: - Expert settings should be accessible but not intrusive\n104: - Document each parameter with tooltip explaining its effect\n105: \n\n(End of file - total 105 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/expert-settings.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n## Overview\nHidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics, balancing parameters, and debugging. Accessible during development and for advanced users to find optimal parametrization.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Access Methods\n```typescript\ninterface ExpertSettingsAccess {\n  keyboardShortcut: string;      // '`' (backtick) for quick access\n  menuPath: string;              // \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu system exists)\n  gesture: string;               // Mobile: triple-tap top-left corner\n}\n```\n\n### Configurable Parameters\n\n#### Movement Detection Parameters\n```typescript","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219111702,"end":1771219111726}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1771219111821,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2cf30001P4RFVCc609xDKO","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2b8e60012Ff0O0tKhOGcBp","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"27ea60c10668e73700104265de6022fd7f0c702e","cost":0,"tokens":{"total":27732,"input":15616,"output":215,"reasoning":108,"cache":{"read":11901,"write":0}}}}
