{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219117351,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2e5170017ezB0IWrJCGN7V","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2cfe3001bP5qprvFn30fFt","type":"tool","callID":"call_de65eea620344ea3b9147f9e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/ui-overlay.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: UI/Overlay System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The UI system provides controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays including a cinematic intro, HUD controls, and responsive interface management for the Game of Life application.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n9: \n10: **Behavior**:\n11: - Shows on app load\n12: - Displays title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n13: - CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n14: - Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n15: \n16: **State**:\n17: ```typescript\n18: interface IntroState {\n19:   isIntro: boolean;    // Showing intro\n20:   isExiting: boolean;  // Playing exit animation\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: **UI State During Intro**:\n25: - Game renders in background\n26: - UI controls hidden\n27: - Audio may play (attract mode)\n28: \n29: ### Main Controls (HUD)\n30: \n31: **Glass HUD Container**:\n32: - Semi-transparent glass effect\n33: - Floating overlay on bottom of screen\n34: - Groups: Main controls, interaction modes, status\n35: \n36: **Main Control Buttons**:\n37: - **PLAY/PAUSE**: Toggle simulation running state\n38: - **STEP**: Execute single generation (disabled while running)\n39: - **RANDOM**: Fill grid randomly (15% cell density)\n40: - **CLEAR**: Remove all cells, reset generation (red text color)\n41: \n42: **Interaction Mode Buttons**:\n43: - **DRAW**: Enable cell placement mode (active state highlighted)\n44: - **ERASE**: Enable cell removal mode (active state highlighted)\n45: \n46: **Status Controls**:\n47: - **Waveform Selector**: Dropdown (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw)\n48: - **Volume Slider**: Range 0-0.5, 0.01 step\n49: - **Generation Counter**: Display \"GEN: {number}\"\n50: - **Settings Toggle**: Gear icon button (⚙️)\n51: \n52: ### Phase Status Display\n53: \n54: **Visibility**: Always visible\n55: \n56: **Layout**:\n57: - Shows current phase: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n58: - Timer display (visible during COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases)\n59: - Flux counter (visible during PLANNING and RUNNING phases)\n60: \n61: ### Settings Panel\n62: \n63: **Access**: Click gear icon in HUD\n64: \n65: **Configuration Options**:\n66: \n67: 1. **Speed**: Slider (10ms to 500ms)\n68: \n69: 2. **Grid Size**: Buttons for Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n70: \n71: 3. **Visuals**:\n72:    - Checkbox: Show grid lines\n73: \n74: 4. **Audio**:\n75:    - Checkbox: Enable sonification\n76: \n77: 5. **Expert Settings**:\n78:    - Access to Expert Settings panel (for tuning game parameters)\n79: \n80: **Close**: × button in header\n81: \n82: ### UI Toggle\n83: \n84: **Toggle Button**:\n85: - Icon frame (minimal)\n86: - Click to show/hide all UI\n87: - Hidden when `enableUI` prop is false (intro mode)\n88: - Position: Fixed corner\n89: \n90: ## Implementation Architecture\n91: \n92: ### State Management\n93: \n94: ```typescript\n95: interface UIState {\n96:   isUiVisible: boolean;        // Master visibility toggle\n97:   isIntro: boolean;            // Intro overlay active\n98:   isExiting: boolean;          // Intro exit animation\n99:   showSettings: boolean;       // Settings panel open\n100:   enableUI: boolean;           // Prop from App (false during intro)\n101: }\n102: ```\n103: \n104: ### Component Hierarchy\n105: \n106: ```\n107: App\n108: ├── IntroOverlay (conditional on isIntro)\n109: ├── GameOfLife\n110: │   ├── CanvasGrid\n111: │   ├── UIToggleButton\n112: │   └── GlassHUDContainer (conditional on enableUI && isUiVisible)\n113: │       ├── GlassHUD\n114: │       └── SettingsPanel (conditional on showSettings)\n115: ```\n116: \n117: ## CSS Architecture\n118: \n119: ### Glass Effect\n120: ```css\n121: .glass-hud {\n122:   background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n123:   backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n124:   border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n125:   border-radius: 12px;\n126: }\n127: ```\n128: \n129: ### Button States\n130: - **Active**: Highlighted background/border\n131: - **Disabled**: Opacity reduced, no pointer events\n132: - **Hover**: Slight brightness increase\n133: \n134: ### Animations\n135: - **Intro Exit**: Scale and fade out over 1.2s\n136: - **Panel Open**: Slide in from side\n137: - **Button Hover**: Scale/brightness transition\n138: \n139: ## Responsive Design\n140: \n141: - **Desktop**: Full width HUD centered at bottom\n142: - **Mobile**: Controls may stack or scroll\n143: - **Touch**: Minimum 44px touch targets\n144: - **Canvas**: Adapts to window size, grid scales accordingly\n145: \n146: ## Edge Cases\n147: \n148: 1. **Intro Exit**: Wait 1.2s for animation before removing component\n149: 2. **UI Hidden**: All controls invisible, toggle button still accessible\n150: 3. **Settings During Run**: Settings apply immediately, no pause required\n151: 4. **Grid Size Change**: Resets simulation\n152: 5. **Clear Grid**: Removes all cells, resets generation\n153: \n154: ## Dependencies\n155: \n156: - All systems: Configurable via settings panel\n157: - Core simulation: Speed and size settings affect simulation\n158: - Audio system: Enable toggle controls sonification\n159: - Canvas rendering: Grid line option\n160: - User interaction: Mode buttons select draw/erase\n161: - Phase management: Phase display shows current game state\n162: \n\n(End of file - total 162 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/ui-overlay.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: UI/Overlay System\n\n## Overview\nThe UI system provides controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays including a cinematic intro, HUD controls, and responsive interface management for the Game of Life application.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n\n**Behavior**:\n- Shows on app load\n- Displays title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n- CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n- Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n\n**State**:\n```typescript\ninterface IntroState {\n  isIntro: boolean;    // Showing intro\n  isExiting: boolean;  // Playing exit animation","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219117338,"end":1771219117349}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219117354,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2e5130018D0YlHoRowiskg","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2cfe3001bP5qprvFn30fFt","type":"tool","callID":"call_aac0afca0edd4ed78a20f45e","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/grid-interaction.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Grid Interaction\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Direct manipulation interface for placing and removing cells on the Game of Life grid during PLANNING phase.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase)\n9: - **Click to Place**: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n10: - **Click to Remove**: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n11: - **Visual Feedback**: Cursor changes to indicate placeable vs non-placeable areas\n12: - **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n13: \n14: ### Interaction Constraints\n15: - Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n16: - Disabled during FINISHED phase\n17: - Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n18: - Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n19: \n20: ### Coordinate System\n21: ```typescript\n22: interface GridInteraction {\n23:   cellX: number;        // 0 to gridWidth-1\n24:   cellY: number;        // 0 to gridHeight-1\n25:   isPlaceable: boolean; // Calculated based on Flux and existing cell\n26: }\n27: ```\n28: \n29: ## UI/UX Requirements\n30: \n31: ### Cursor States\n32: - **Default**: Standard cursor\n33: - **Over Empty Cell (Placeable)**: Crosshair or cell preview outline\n34: - **Over Empty Cell (Unplaceable)**: Forbidden symbol (Flux = 0)\n35: - **Over Live Cell (Removable)**: Minus icon or highlight\n36: \n37: ### Visual Feedback\n38: - **Cell Preview**: Ghost/outline of cell follows cursor when hovering over grid\n39: - **Cell Placement**: Fade-in animation (0.1s duration)\n40: - **Cell Removal**: Shrink animation (0.15s duration)\n41: - **Invalid Action**: Brief red flash on cursor location\n42: \n43: ### Mobile Considerations\n44: - Pinch-to-zoom disabled on game grid\n45: - Touch-and-hold to drag not needed (single click only)\n46: - Prevent accidental browser zoom on double-tap\n47: - Visual ripple effect on touch\n48: \n49: ## Edge Cases\n50: \n51: 1. **Rapid Clicking**: User might click faster than animation - ensure state consistency\n52: 2. **Edge of Grid**: Clicking exactly on grid boundary should round to nearest cell\n53: 3. **Overlapping with UI**: Ensure grid doesn't extend under HUD elements\n54: 4. **Window Resize**: Grid cells must maintain aspect ratio on resize\n55: \n56: ## Implementation Notes\n57: \n58: - Use event delegation for grid click handling\n59: - Calculate cell coordinates from mouse/touch position: `cellX = Math.floor((x - gridOffsetX) / cellSize)`\n60: - Consider using CSS Grid or Canvas for rendering - Canvas may be better for performance with many cells\n61: - Implement hit testing to distinguish between grid cells and gaps\n62: \n\n(End of file - total 62 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/grid-interaction.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Grid Interaction\n\n## Overview\nDirect manipulation interface for placing and removing cells on the Game of Life grid during PLANNING phase.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Placement Mode (PLANNING Phase)\n- **Click to Place**: Single click on empty grid cell places a live cell\n- **Click to Remove**: Single click on existing live cell removes it and refunds Flux\n- **Visual Feedback**: Cursor changes to indicate placeable vs non-placeable areas\n- **Minimum Cells Rule**: START button disabled until at least 1 cell has been placed\n\n### Interaction Constraints\n- Disabled entirely during RUNNING phase\n- Disabled during FINISHED phase\n- Grid cells must be clickable on both desktop (mouse) and mobile (touch)\n- Touch targets minimum 44x44px for mobile accessibility\n\n### Coordinate System","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219117333,"end":1771219117352}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219117356,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2e50e001zZlvYFLLWBsraS","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2cfe3001bP5qprvFn30fFt","type":"tool","callID":"call_b19724f8c3ff4b8492cbc47a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/user-interaction.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: User Interaction System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The user interaction system handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid with real-time visual feedback and sound generation.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Interaction Modes\n9: ```typescript\n10: type InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n11: ```\n12: \n13: **Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n14: **Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n15: \n16: ### Mouse Interaction\n17: \n18: #### Mouse Down\n19: 1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n20: 2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n21: 3. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n22: \n23: #### Mouse Move (while pressed)\n24: 1. Capture mouse position\n25: 2. Convert to grid coordinates\n26: 3. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n27: \n28: #### Mouse Up (global)\n29: 1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n30: 2. Prevent stale drag state\n31: \n32: ### Touch Interaction\n33: \n34: #### Touch Start\n35: 1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n36: 2. Capture first touch position\n37: 3. Convert to grid coordinates\n38: 4. Trigger interaction handler with type='down'\n39: \n40: #### Touch Move\n41: 1. Prevent default (stop scrolling)\n42: 2. Capture first touch position\n43: 3. Convert to grid coordinates\n44: 4. Trigger interaction handler with type='enter'\n45: \n46: #### Touch End / Cancel\n47: 1. Set `isMouseDown` state to false\n48: \n49: ## Implementation Architecture\n50: \n51: ### Coordinate Mapping\n52: ```typescript\n53: interface GridCoordinates {\n54:   row: number; // 0 to numRows-1\n55:   col: number; // 0 to numCols-1\n56: }\n57: \n58: function getCellFromEvent(\n59:   event: MouseEvent | TouchEvent,\n60:   canvas: HTMLCanvasElement,\n61:   numRows: number,\n62:   numCols: number\n63: ): GridCoordinates\n64: ```\n65: \n66: ### Interaction Handler\n67: ```typescript\n68: function handleCellInteract(\n69:   row: number,\n70:   col: number,\n71:   type: 'down' | 'enter'\n72: ): void\n73: ```\n74: \n75: - **type='down'**: Modify cell(s)\n76: - **type='enter'**: Only modify if mouse down\n77: \n78: ### Sound Integration\n79: - **Draw/Erase**: Play interaction sound (different tones)\n80: - **Sound Engine**: Called per cell interaction\n81: \n82: ## Edge Cases\n83: \n84: 1. **Boundary Coordinates**: Math.floor() ensures valid indices\n85: 2. **Rapid Clicking**: Multiple clicks allowed\n86: 3. **Canvas Resize**: Grid dimensions update, coordinates recalculate\n87: 4. **Touch Conflicts**: PreventDefault() blocks browser zoom/scroll\n88: 5. **Mouse Leave Canvas**: Set isMouseDown to false to stop drag\n89: \n90: ## Mobile Considerations\n91: \n92: - **Touch Action**: `touch-action: none` on canvas element\n93: - **Target Size**: Responsive cell size (18px mobile, 20px desktop) meets minimum touch target\n94: - **Prevent Default**: Stop scrolling while drawing\n95: - **Multi-touch**: Only first touch used (ignore additional touches)\n96: \n97: ## Visual Feedback\n98: \n99: - **Cursor**: `crosshair` style over canvas\n100: - **Hover Effects**: None (draw directly on grid)\n101: - **Selection Feedback**: No preview shown (immediate drawing)\n102: \n103: ## Dependencies\n104: \n105: - Core simulation engine: Grid ref and dimensions\n106: - Audio sonification system: Play interaction sounds\n107: - Canvas rendering system: Redraw on state change\n108: \n\n(End of file - total 108 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/user-interaction.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: User Interaction System\n\n## Overview\nThe user interaction system handles mouse and touch input for drawing and erasing cells on the grid with real-time visual feedback and sound generation.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Interaction Modes\n```typescript\ntype InteractionMode = 'draw' | 'erase';\n```\n\n**Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n**Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n\n### Mouse Interaction\n\n#### Mouse Down\n1. Capture mouse position relative to canvas\n2. Convert to grid coordinates: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219117328,"end":1771219117354}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219117360,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2e51c001vzaAoaETvx5F0k","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2cfe3001bP5qprvFn30fFt","type":"tool","callID":"call_26d6ec5a668f4cd79bc81cf4","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/phase-management.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Phase Management\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: State machine governing the three core game phases: PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Phase Definitions\n9: \n10: #### PLANNING Phase\n11: - **Entry Condition**: Level initialization or restart\n12: - **Duration**: Unlimited (player controls when to start)\n13: - **Allowed Actions**: Place/remove cells using Flux\n14: - **START Button**: Visible and enabled when ≥1 cell placed\n15: - **Exit Condition**: Player clicks START button\n16: \n17: #### RUNNING Phase\n18: - **Entry Condition**: Countdown finishes (3, 2, 1...) after player clicked START\n19: - **Duration**: Fixed countdown timer (level-specific, starts at 45s base)\n20: - **Allowed Actions**: Cell placement using saved Flux (add-only)\n21: - **Simulation**: Game of Life rules execute automatically\n22: - **Exit Conditions**:\n23:    - Timer reaches 0 → FINISHED (score finalization)\n24:    - All cells die → FINISHED (score stops accumulating, level ends)\n25: \n26: #### FINISHED Phase\n27: - **Entry Condition**: Timer expires or all cells die\n28: - **Duration**: Brief pause before auto-advance (2.0s)\n29: - **Allowed Actions**: None (view-only)\n30: - **Outcome Display**: Show score, cells alive\n31: - **Exit Condition**: Auto-advance after 2.0s (fade transition to next level)\n32: - **Simulation**: Stops completely, no carryover to next level\n33: \n34: ### State Machine\n35: ```typescript\n36: type GamePhase = 'PLANNING' | 'RUNNING' | 'FINISHED';\n37: \n38: interface PhaseState {\n39:   current: GamePhase;\n40:   canTransition: boolean;\n41:   blockers: string[]; // Reasons why transition blocked\n42: }\n43: \n44: const transitions = {\n45:   'PLANNING': ['COUNTDOWN', 'RUNNING'],\n46:   'COUNTDOWN': ['RUNNING'],\n47:   'RUNNING': ['FINISHED'],\n48:   'FINISHED': ['PLANNING'] // Auto-triggered, circular to next level\n49: };\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ## UI/UX Requirements\n53: \n54: ### Phase Indicators\n55: - **PLANNING**:\n56:    - \"Place your cells\" text or icon\n57:    - START button prominent (enabled when ≥1 cell placed)\n58:    - Flux counter visible\n59: - **COUNTDOWN**:\n60:    - Large \"3... 2... 1...\" display\n61:    - No input accepted\n62:    - Simulation NOT running yet\n63: - **RUNNING**:\n64:    - Timer prominently displayed (countdown)\n65:    - \"Simulation Running\" indicator\n66:    - Score ticking up in real-time\n67:    - Flux counter visible (if any saved)\n68: - **FINISHED**:\n69:    - \"Time's Up\" or \"Level Complete\" message\n70:    - Final score display\n71:    - Brief stats (cells alive)\n72:    - Auto-advance countdown indicator\n73: \n74: ### Phase Transitions\n75: - **PLANNING → COUNTDOWN**:\n76:    - Player clicks START button\n77:    - Immediate transition to countdown\n78: - **COUNTDOWN → RUNNING**:\n79:    - \"3, 2, 1\" countdown completes\n80:    - Simulation starts immediately\n81:    - Sound effect: \"Simulation starting\"\n82: - **RUNNING → FINISHED**:\n83:    - Timer hits 0 OR all cells die\n84:    - Simulation stops immediately\n85:    - Sound effect: \"Level complete\" or timer expiration\n86: - **FINISHED → PLANNING** (next level):\n87:    - Fade out current screen (2.0s)\n88:    - Fade in new level (2.0s)\n89:    - Fresh grid, fresh Flux, no carryover\n90: \n91: ## Edge Cases\n92: \n93: 1. **Zero Cells at Start**: START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n94: 2. **All Cells Die Early**: Level ends immediately, score stops, advances to next level\n95: 3. **Browser Tab Switch**: Timer continues running when tab inactive\n96: 4. **Rapid Phase Switching**: Prevent clicking START multiple times rapidly\n97: 5. **Countdown Interrupted**: No input allowed during countdown phase\n98: 6. **Level Transition**: No simulation carryover between levels - fresh start each level\n99: \n100: ## Implementation Notes\n101: \n102: - Use React useReducer for phase state management\n103: - Add COUNTDOWN phase between PLANNING and RUNNING\n104: - Phase transitions should be guarded (can't skip phases)\n105: - Timer must use accurate timing (Date.now() or performance.now())\n106: - Simulation must NOT start until countdown completes\n107: - Level transition stops simulation completely - no carryover\n108: - Consider using a state machine library like XState if complexity grows\n109: - Log phase transitions for debugging\n110: \n\n(End of file - total 110 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/phase-management.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Phase Management\n\n## Overview\nState machine governing the three core game phases: PLANNING → RUNNING → FINISHED.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Phase Definitions\n\n#### PLANNING Phase\n- **Entry Condition**: Level initialization or restart\n- **Duration**: Unlimited (player controls when to start)\n- **Allowed Actions**: Place/remove cells using Flux\n- **START Button**: Visible and enabled when ≥1 cell placed\n- **Exit Condition**: Player clicks START button\n\n#### RUNNING Phase\n- **Entry Condition**: Countdown finishes (3, 2, 1...) after player clicked START\n- **Duration**: Fixed countdown timer (level-specific, starts at 45s base)\n- **Allowed Actions**: Cell placement using saved Flux (add-only)","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219117342,"end":1771219117357}}}}
