{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219122044,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2f76a001nPT9lqkfFv7SSu","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2e5ed001ispAF4XjBa3tlz","type":"tool","callID":"call_4b91b3097f7e4cd781091923","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/scoring-system.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/scoring-system.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Scoring System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Real-time score calculation based on cellular pattern classifications, with points awarded per generation.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Scoring Formula\n9: ```typescript\n10: interface ScoringConfig {\n11:   moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n12:   oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n13:   staticPointsPerGeneration: number;     // Always 0\n14:   scoreMultiplier: number;                 // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n15: }\n16: \n17: interface ScoreState {\n18:   currentScore: number;\n19:   generationScore: number;      // Score earned this generation\n20:   totalPatternsTracked: number; // Stats: total patterns ever detected\n21: }\n22: ```\n23: \n24: ### Per-Generation Calculation\n25: For each generation during RUNNING phase:\n26: \n27: ```typescript\n28: function calculateGenerationScore(\n29:   trackedClusters: TrackedCluster[],\n30:   config: ScoringConfig\n31: ): number {\n32:   let generationScore = 0;\n33:   \n34:   for (const cluster of trackedClusters) {\n35:     switch (cluster.classification) {\n36:       case 'MOVER':\n37:         generationScore += config.moverPointsPerGeneration;\n38:         break;\n39:       case 'OSCILLATOR':\n40:         generationScore += config.oscillatorPointsPerGeneration;\n41:         break;\n42:       case 'STATIC':\n43:         // No points for static patterns\n44:         break;\n45:     }\n46:   }\n47:   \n48:   return generationScore * config.scoreMultiplier;\n49: }\n50: \n51: // Update score each generation\n52: scoreState.currentScore += calculateGenerationScore(clusters, config);\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Scoring Visibility\n56: - Real-time: Score updates every generation during RUNNING phase\n57: - Smooth animation: Number counting up effect (lerp over 0.2s)\n58: - Milestones: Brief flash every 100 points (optional)\n59: \n60: ## UI/UX Requirements\n61: \n62: ### Score Display\n63: - **Location**: Top-left of screen\n64: - **Format**: Large number with \"PTS\" label\n65: - **Animation**: \n66:   - Smooth increment when score changes\n67:   - Brief pulse/flash on point gain\n68:   - Color: White/bright, stands out from grid\n69: \n70: ### Pattern Breakdown (Optional)\n71: - Small sub-display showing:\n72:   - Active Movers: [count]\n73:   - Active Oscillators: [count]\n74:   - Current Rate: [points/gen]\n75: \n76: ### End-of-Level Stats\n77: Display on FINISHED phase:\n78: - Final Score: [number]\n79: - Time Survived: [seconds]\n80: - Patterns Created: [count]\n81: \n82: ## Edge Cases\n83: \n84: 1. **Score Overflow**: Cap score at MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (9,007,199,254,740,991) to prevent overflow issues\n85: 2. **Negative Multiplier**: Expert settings validation should prevent negative multipliers\n86: 3. **Zero Points Generation**: Possible if no patterns active - ensure UI handles gracefully\n87: 4. **Score Calculation Lag**: If tracking takes >16ms, could delay score update - decouple from render\n88: \n89: ## Score Persistence\n90: \n91: **Per-Level Reset**: Score resets to 0 at the start of each level (no carry-over)\n92: **High Score Tracking**: Save highest score achieved per level to localStorage for player progress tracking\n93: \n94: ## Implementation Notes\n95: \n96: - Scoring must be deterministic (same patterns = same score)\n97: - Calculate in separate thread or use requestIdleCallback if heavy\n98: - Store config in expert settings with defaults:\n99:   - moverPointsPerGeneration: 10 (high reward for movement)\n100:   - oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 2 (small reward for activity)\n101:   - staticPointsPerGeneration: 0 (no reward)\n102:   - scoreMultiplier: 1.0\n103: \n\n(End of file - total 103 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/scoring-system.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Scoring System\n\n## Overview\nReal-time score calculation based on cellular pattern classifications, with points awarded per generation.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Scoring Formula\n```typescript\ninterface ScoringConfig {\n  moverPointsPerGeneration: number;      // Default: 10, range: 1-100\n  oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: number;   // Default: 2, range: 0-20\n  staticPointsPerGeneration: number;     // Always 0\n  scoreMultiplier: number;                 // Default: 1.0, range: 0.1-5.0\n}\n\ninterface ScoreState {\n  currentScore: number;\n  generationScore: number;      // Score earned this generation\n  totalPatternsTracked: number; // Stats: total patterns ever detected","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219122028,"end":1771219122041}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219122046,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2f76e001UgP6THILgxKWZ6","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2e5ed001ispAF4XjBa3tlz","type":"tool","callID":"call_e023c23e85c64ed5b3b40745","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/movement-detection.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/movement-detection.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Movement Detection (Centroid Tracking)\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: Algorithmic system to detect and classify cellular movement patterns by tracking centroids of connected cell clusters over time.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Connected Component Detection\n9: Identify clusters of adjacent live cells using 8-connectivity (include diagonals):\n10: \n11: ```typescript\n12: interface CellCluster {\n13:   id: string;                    // Unique identifier (e.g., hash of coordinates)\n14:   cells: Set<string>;             // Set of \"x,y\" coordinate strings\n15:   centroid: { x: number; y: number };  // Average of all cell positions\n16:   generation: number;             // When this cluster was first identified\n17: }\n18: \n19: function findConnectedComponents(grid: boolean[][]): CellCluster[];\n20: ```\n21: \n22: ### Centroid Tracking\n23: Track cluster centroids across generations to calculate velocity:\n24: \n25: ```typescript\n26: interface TrackedCluster extends CellCluster {\n27:   centroidHistory: { x: number; y: number }[];  // Last N centroids\n28:   velocity: { dx: number; dy: number };         // Calculated movement vector\n29:   classification: 'MOVER' | 'OSCILLATOR' | 'STATIC';\n30: }\n31: \n32: interface TrackingConfig {\n33:   historyLength: number;        // Generations to track (expert setting, default: 5)\n34:   movementThreshold: number;      // Min distance to be considered moving (default: 0.5 cells)\n35: }\n36: ```\n37: \n38: ### Classification Algorithm\n39: For each cluster with sufficient history:\n40: \n41: 1. **Calculate Centroid Velocity**: \n42:    - `dx = (current.x - history[0].x) / historyLength`\n43:    - `dy = (current.y - history[0].y) / historyLength`\n44: \n45: 2. **Classify**:\n46:    - **MOVER**: `|dx| > threshold` OR `|dy| > threshold` (centroid is translating)\n47:    - **OSCILLATOR**: Centroid static (within threshold) BUT cell set changes between generations (cells are moving locally)\n48:    - **STATIC**: Centroid static AND cell set unchanged\n49: \n50: 3. **Cluster Persistence**:\n51:    - Match clusters across generations by nearest centroid\n52:    - Handle cluster splits/merges (edge case: when two gliders collide)\n53: \n54: ## UI/UX Requirements\n55: \n56: ### Performance Indicators\n57: - Show \"active patterns\" count in HUD\n58: - Highlight moving patterns with subtle glow effect\n59: \n60: ## Edge Cases\n61: \n62:  1. **Cluster Split**: One cluster becomes two (e.g., glider collision) - track both as new clusters or attempt lineage?\n63:  2. **Cluster Merge**: Two clusters become one - classification reset to avoid double-counting\n64:  3. **Oscillator Period Detection**: Blinker has period 2, Pulsar has period 3 - centroid stays same but cells swap\n65:  4. **Glider Guns**: Stationary structure producing moving gliders - gun is Static, produced gliders are Movers\n66:  5. **Minimum Cluster Size**: Single isolated cell - treat as cluster of size 1 or ignore?\n67:  6. **Large Grid Performance**: With 100x100 grid (performance benchmark, not a game configuration), expect ~50-200 clusters max - must process in < 16ms for 60fps\n68: \n69: ## Implementation Notes\n70: \n71: - Run connected component analysis every generation during RUNNING phase\n72: - Store cluster history in circular buffer (efficient memory usage)\n73: - Use Manhattan distance or Euclidean for centroid matching\n74: - Performance requirements must scale with actual game grid sizes (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n75: - Optimization: Only recompute centroids for changed regions, not full grid\n76: - Memory: Limit history buffer size to prevent unbounded growth\n77: \n\n(End of file - total 77 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/movement-detection.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Movement Detection (Centroid Tracking)\n\n## Overview\nAlgorithmic system to detect and classify cellular movement patterns by tracking centroids of connected cell clusters over time.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Connected Component Detection\nIdentify clusters of adjacent live cells using 8-connectivity (include diagonals):\n\n```typescript\ninterface CellCluster {\n  id: string;                    // Unique identifier (e.g., hash of coordinates)\n  cells: Set<string>;             // Set of \"x,y\" coordinate strings\n  centroid: { x: number; y: number };  // Average of all cell positions\n  generation: number;             // When this cluster was first identified\n}\n\nfunction findConnectedComponents(grid: boolean[][]): CellCluster[];\n```","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219122031,"end":1771219122043}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219122048,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2f774001rQwPKLvCmun06q","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2e5ed001ispAF4XjBa3tlz","type":"tool","callID":"call_35eaabbc258f47ea9f20c9c3","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/audio-sonification.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Audio Sonification System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The audio sonification system generates real-time sounds based on simulation birth events and user interactions using the Web Audio API, providing audio feedback for cellular automaton behavior.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Sound Engine Interface\n9: \n10: ```typescript\n11: interface SoundEngine {\n12:   setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void;\n13:   setVolume(volume: number): void;\n14:   setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void;\n15:   playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void;\n16:   playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void;\n17: }\n18: ```\n19: \n20: ### Generation Sounds\n21: \n22: **Trigger**: After each simulation step with bornCount > 0\n23: \n24: **Pitch Mapping**:\n25: - Based on average row position of new births\n26: - Formula: `pitch = (1 - avgRow / totalRows) * frequencyRange`\n27: - Higher rows (top) = higher pitch\n28: - Lower rows (bottom) = lower pitch\n29: \n30: **Intensity Mapping**:\n31: - Based on number of births: bornCount\n32: - More births = louder/more prominent sound\n33: \n34: **Waveform Types**:\n35: - `sine`: Smooth, pure tone (default)\n36: - `triangle`: Slightly richer harmonics\n37: - `square`: Harsh, buzzy tone\n38: - `sawtooth`: Bright, brassy tone\n39: \n40: ### Interaction Sounds\n41: \n42: **Draw Sound**:\n43: - Triggered when placing a cell\n44: - Higher pitch, short duration\n45: \n46: **Erase Sound**:\n47: - Triggered when removing a cell\n48: - Lower pitch, short duration\n49: \n50: ### Volume Control\n51: \n52: - **Range**: 0.0 to 0.5\n53: - **Default**: 0.1 (10%)\n54: - **UI Slider**: 10ms steps, displays percentage (volume * 200%)\n55: \n56: ## Implementation Architecture\n57: \n58: ### Audio Context\n59: \n60: ```typescript\n61: class SoundEngine {\n62:   private audioContext: AudioContext | null = null;\n63:   private enabled: boolean = true;\n64:   private volume: number = 0.1;\n65:   private waveform: OscillatorType = 'sine';\n66: \n67:   // ... methods\n68: }\n69: ```\n70: \n71: ### Sound Generation Process\n72: \n73: 1. **Initialize Context**: Create on first user interaction (browser requirement)\n74: 2. **Create Oscillator**: Generate sound with configured waveform\n75: 3. **Create Gain Node**: Control volume and envelope\n76: 4. **Connect Nodes**: Oscillator → Gain → Destination\n77: 5. **Set Parameters**: Frequency based on data, volume from setting\n78: 6. **Envelope**: Quick attack, exponential decay\n79: 7. **Cleanup**: Stop and disconnect after sound completes\n80: \n81: ### Lazy Initialization\n82: \n83: - AudioContext created on first sound play\n84: - Handles browser autoplay policies\n85: - Resumes context if suspended\n86: \n87: ## Audio Parameters\n88: \n89: ### Generation Sound\n90: ```typescript\n91: interface GenerationSoundParams {\n92:   frequency: number;    // Derived from row position\n93:   duration: number;     // Short, ~100-200ms\n94:   volume: number;       // baseVolume * bornCount scaling\n95:   waveform: OscillatorType;\n96: }\n97: ```\n98: \n99: ### Interaction Sound\n100: ```typescript\n101: interface InteractionSoundParams {\n102:   drawFrequency: number;    // Higher pitch (~880Hz)\n103:   eraseFrequency: number;   // Lower pitch (~440Hz)\n104:   duration: number;         // Very short (~50ms)\n105:   volume: number;          // baseVolume\n106:   waveform: OscillatorType;\n107: }\n108: ```\n109: \n110: ## Edge Cases\n111: \n112: 1. **No Births**: Sound not triggered\n113: 2. **Suspended Context**: Resume on next interaction\n114: 3. **Volume = 0**: Sounds generated but at 0 gain\n115: 4. **Disabled**: Engine returns early without generating sounds\n116: 5. **Multiple Events**: Concurrent sounds allowed (polyphonic)\n117: \n118: ## Browser Compatibility\n119: \n120: - Requires Web Audio API support\n121: - Modern browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n122: - iOS: Requires user gesture to start\n123: - Autoplay policy: Context starts suspended\n124: \n125: ## Dependencies\n126: \n127: - Core simulation engine: Provides birth statistics\n128: - User interaction system: Triggers draw/erase sounds\n129: - UI/overlay system: Volume, waveform, enabled settings\n130: \n\n(End of file - total 130 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/audio-sonification.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Audio Sonification System\n\n## Overview\nThe audio sonification system generates real-time sounds based on simulation birth events and user interactions using the Web Audio API, providing audio feedback for cellular automaton behavior.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Sound Engine Interface\n\n```typescript\ninterface SoundEngine {\n  setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void;\n  setVolume(volume: number): void;\n  setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void;\n  playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void;\n  playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void;\n}\n```\n\n### Generation Sounds","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219122038,"end":1771219122044}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771219122049,"sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","part":{"id":"prt_c64e2f771001GRLoPDdVxnYKUA","sessionID":"ses_39b1d5975ffec3v86BDnLsDzO3","messageID":"msg_c64e2e5ed001ispAF4XjBa3tlz","type":"tool","callID":"call_95261baf2ccf4c8989ac4544","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/canvas-rendering.md"},"output":"<path>/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/specs/canvas-rendering.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Spec: Canvas Rendering System\n2: \n3: ## Overview\n4: The canvas rendering system draws the Game of Life grid with age-based neon color gradients and glow effects using HTML5 Canvas for high-performance rendering.\n5: \n6: ## Functional Requirements\n7: \n8: ### Rendering Theme\n9: **Dark Neon Theme**:\n10: - Background: `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n11: - Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (subtle, only during PLANNING phase)\n12: \n13: **Cell Age-Based Colors**:\n14: - Age 0 (just born): `#00ffff` (bright cyan, intense glow)\n15: - Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue, medium glow)\n16: - Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta/pink, subtle glow)\n17: - Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (deep purple, minimal glow)\n18: \n19: **Glow Effects**:\n20: - Age 0: Shadow blur = 15px (highly visible)\n21: - Age 1-2: Shadow blur = 8px\n22: - Age 3-5: Shadow blur = 4px\n23: - Age 6+: Shadow blur = 2px\n24: \n25: ### Cell Rendering\n26: - **Cell Size**: Responsive (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n27: - **Age-Based Colors**: Color computed from cell state value\n28: - **Glow Effects**: Shadow blur and shadow color applied\n29: - **Shape**: Square with slight corner radius (2px)\n30: \n31: ### Grid Lines\n32: - **Visibility**: Toggleable (keyboard shortcut: 'G' key), only shown when not running\n33: - **Color**: `#1a1a2e` (subtle)\n34: - **Stroke Width**: 1px\n35: - **Position**: Around each cell\n36: - **Default**: Hidden during RUNNING phase, visible during PLANNING phase\n37: \n38: ## Implementation Architecture\n39: \n40: ### Canvas Setup\n41: ```typescript\n42: interface CanvasConfig {\n43:   width: number;  // numCols * cellSize\n44:   height: number; // numRows * cellSize\n45:   dpr: number;   // window.devicePixelRatio\n46:   cellSize: number; // 18px (mobile) or 20px (desktop)\n47: }\n48: ```\n49: \n50: ### Responsive Cell Sizing\n51: - Mobile devices (screen width < 768px): 18px cells\n52: - Desktop devices (screen width >= 768px): 20px cells\n53: - Cell size updates on window resize\n54: - Grid dimensions recalculate based on cell size\n55: \n56: ### Rendering Pipeline\n57: 1. **Canvas Resize**: Update width/height if dimensions changed\n58: 2. **Transform Reset**: Clear and apply DPR scaling\n59: 3. **Draw Loop**:\n60:    - Clear canvas with background color\n61:    - Draw grid lines (if enabled)\n62:    - Draw live cells with age-based styling and glow\n63: 4. **Intensity Update**: Set CSS variable `--life-intensity`\n64: \n65: ### Performance Optimizations\n66: - **DPR Scaling**: Use `window.devicePixelRatio` for sharp rendering\n67: - **Transform Reset**: Clear transform before resize\n68: - **Optimized Draws**: Minimize context state changes\n69: - **Dependency Tracking**: useCallback on [numRows, numCols, cellSize]\n70: \n71: ## Visual Effects\n72: \n73: ### Glow/Shadows\n74: ```typescript\n75: interface CellShadow {\n76:   blur: number;    // 2px to 15px based on age\n77:   color: string;  // Matches cell color\n78: }\n79: ```\n80: \n81: ### Intensity Metric\n82: ```typescript\n83: const intensity = Math.min(activeCount / 500, 1);\n84: document.documentElement.style.setProperty('--life-intensity', intensity.toString());\n85: ```\n86: - Used for CSS-based ambient effects\n87: - Scaled from 0-500 cells\n88: \n89: ## Edge Cases\n90: \n91: 1. **Canvas Resize**: Must handle width/height update, DPR scaling, and cell size recalculation together\n92: 2. **Empty Grid**: Draws only grid lines (if enabled)\n93: 3. **High Cell Count**: May have performance issues with 500+ cells\n94: 4. **Rapid Cell Size Changes**: Color computations cached per frame\n95: \n96: ## Mobile Considerations\n97: \n98: - Touch coordinates mapped to canvas space\n99: - Prevent browser zoom on canvas interaction\n100: - Maintain 18px cell size on mobile\n101: - Ensure minimum 10 cells visible in smallest dimension\n102: \n103: ## Dependencies\n104: \n105: - Core simulation engine: Provides grid state and dimensions\n106: - UI/overlay system: Grid line toggle setting\n107: - User interaction system: Triggers redraws on cell changes\n108: \n\n(End of file - total 108 lines)\n</content>","title":"specs/canvas-rendering.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Spec: Canvas Rendering System\n\n## Overview\nThe canvas rendering system draws the Game of Life grid with age-based neon color gradients and glow effects using HTML5 Canvas for high-performance rendering.\n\n## Functional Requirements\n\n### Rendering Theme\n**Dark Neon Theme**:\n- Background: `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n- Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (subtle, only during PLANNING phase)\n\n**Cell Age-Based Colors**:\n- Age 0 (just born): `#00ffff` (bright cyan, intense glow)\n- Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue, medium glow)\n- Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta/pink, subtle glow)\n- Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (deep purple, minimal glow)\n\n**Glow Effects**:\n- Age 0: Shadow blur = 15px (highly visible)","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771219122034,"end":1771219122046}}}}
